From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] main: dismiss Frame when a zoom shortcut changes view

The GTK4 Frame is an overlay. Direct F1-F4 capture changed the stack level but
left the Frame panels revealed, making the destination view appear blank or
obscured. Match Sugar's zoom action semantics by dismissing the Frame before
switching the desktop view.

---
 src/jarabe/main.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/jarabe/main.py b/src/jarabe/main.py
--- a/src/jarabe/main.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/main.py
@@ -336,6 +336,8 @@ def _setup_main_window(shell_instance):
             level = zoom_keys.get(keyval)
             if level is None:
                 return False
+            from jarabe import frame
+            frame.get_view().hide()
             shell_instance.set_zoom_level(level)
             return True
